{"name":"Marquee White","hex":"#f5ead6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marquee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large tent with open sides, used for outdoors entertainment.","A projecting canopy over an entrance, especially one with a sign that displays the name of the establishment or other information of it."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Most famous; preeminent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marquee"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marquee (structure)","blocks":[{"text":"A marquee is most commonly a structure placed over the entrance to a hotel, theatre, casino, train station, or similar building. It often has signage stating either the name of the establishment or, in the case of theatres, the play or movie and the artist(s) appearing at that venue. The marquee is sometimes identifiable by a surrounding compound of light bulbs, usually yellow or white, that flash intermittently or as chasing lights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/View_of_the_Apollo_Theatre_marquee%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_between_1946_and_1948_%28William_P._Gottlieb_00141%29.jpg/330px-View_of_the_Apollo_Theatre_marquee%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_between_1946_and_1948_%28William_P._Gottlieb_00141%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marquee_(structure)","wikidata":"Q11170170"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg/500px-Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg/1280px-Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg/500px-Madison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A marquee outside The Anthem advertises a sold-out Bon Iver concert","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadison_House_Presents_Bon_Iver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Exterior_of_Earl%27s_Court_Station%2C_London%2C_1973.jpg/500px-Exterior_of_Earl%27s_Court_Station%2C_London%2C_1973.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Exterior_of_Earl%27s_Court_Station%2C_London%2C_1973.jpg/500px-Exterior_of_Earl%27s_Court_Station%2C_London%2C_1973.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marquee outside Earl